From d13d8057935245c2d7bfe15a81a756b4fd7315a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:52:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/91] moe-stream : the drop rule on by default (0.14 with
 DROP_ALL), and C13 - a heavy expert only on the drive replaced by the
 best-scoring held one (SiegeLadder, both lossy; C13 off by default)

The drop rule (an expert held in neither VRAM nor the host tier, below 0.14 of its token's routing weight, is not waited
for and is read into the tier for later) is the default since the user's decision of 18.10: on ds4's general-100 and
router-112 it is within the statistical error of the exact build (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.46, 4.64) and +4.7% over
runahead; "check the accuracy later" - Test 6. With LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_DROP_W unset it is 0.14 with DROP_ALL (the call
must be freed from the drive); LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_DROP_W=0 is the exact path, where runahead is on by default as before;
an explicit DROP_W keeps its old meaning. The start-up log says which.

C13 (LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_SUBST, the user's idea of 18.10): inside the remap, next to the drop rule, a routed expert on the
drive whose share is at least the drop threshold (any share with the rule off) is replaced in each of its pairs by the
best-scoring expert of the token (router selection score) that the card holds resident or the host tier holds whole,
and is read into the tier for later; light ones are still dropped, so the call need not wait for the drive. Mode 1: no
slot and not in the tier; mode 2: also a slot still loading from the drive. LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_SUBST_W=1 gives the
substitute its own renormalised probability (default: the original's weight). The selection scores and probabilities
ride in the remap's single packed input (no extra card input or synchronize); with SUBST unset the graph and every path
are as before. One counter line "C13 substitute". The wave plan now also clears the drop rule's list, which the trace of
a prompt chunk after a decode call used to repeat (an old quirk the default rule would have made common).

Measured (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.68-4.69): the exact path unchanged - KL 0 (max 5.2e-5) against the k5 base, and
router-112's case_111 bit-identical to the build of 17.10; the default's KL 0.0174 at -ub 1 (more than before P9: kl_run's
512-token calls start P9's prompt holding); C13 mode 1 with runahead KL 0.0187, mode 2 KL 0.199 (next to runahead most
staged experts are still loading when their call comes - not a generation mode). A review agent found no crash, hang or
output defect.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
